  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Warmer and more humid conditions return into \nmidweek with highest odds for rain Thursday \n\nLatest CAMs support a modest increase in POPs across the northern\ntier of CPA late tonight into early Wednesday morning. Temps, \ndewpoints, and precip probs trend higher on Wednesday and peak \non Thursday. A weak frontal boundary sinking southeast from the\nLower Great Lakes will interact with the warmer/higher dewpoint\nair and trigger scattered showers and a few t-storms through\nmidweek. At this time, severe storms are not expected with only\na limited/marginal risk of locally heavy rainfall across the\nwestern Alleghenies.  \n\nConfidence in a dry end to the week has increased as slightly\ncooler and drier/lower pwat air arrives from the north behind\nthe aforementioned front. Precip trends from later in the \nweekend into early next week are wetter on the margin for this \ncycle and will need to monitor for potential +RA signal.",
